  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Zernaki tepe, just N Erci\u015f</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient place in Van province, Turkey. It had a street grid, fortifications of mud brick on a polygonal masonry foundation, and at least 14 building inscriptions in Aramaic from the Parthian period. Professor Rafet \u00c7avu\u015fo\u011flu began a program of excavations in 2021, which appears to be unpublished as of October 2025.",
